<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of text in a single column of verse, with the page number and running head at the top. A catchword "Hic" stands at the lower right, below the last line.</layout>
  <page_number>68</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Hic</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Quòd rite veris Numen honoribus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Votisque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>semper supplicibus colis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Quod inssa[?] feruas, &amp; potenti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Te geris vsque Deo minorem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Quid tuta virtus praesidio Patris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Possit supremi, quid queat indoles</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Addicta Christo, Principisve</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Quid valeant pia vota iusti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Hostilis ardens agminis impetus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Senfit retusus nuper, &amp; aemula</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Senfere, quae trifti cohortes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Cortracia[?] cecidere pugna:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Sensitque Ductor, funera qui tibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Audax parabat dura IOVESIVS:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Quum vota rififfet piorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Sollicitasque preces superbus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Nam vitta spreto Numine brachiis Fidens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>iuuentus cum Duce corruit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Vicitque cœlestem precatus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Miles opem metuendus hosti.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Sic praepotenti Ieffaides prece</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Pugnauit olim, quum rudis agminum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Fudit Philistæas phalanges,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Atque trucem feriit Gigantem:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>Quem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>mole vasta corporis ardui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Armabat ensis, cuspis &amp; anea</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Ingentis hastae: cuique pectus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>Ære ferox solido misabat.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="Quem mole vasta" line_from="26" line_to="26">Hic</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>The printed word after "inssa" is uncertain (long s and ff forms); "inssa[?]" is a best reading. "Cortracia" may be a misprint for "Contracia"; kept as printed with [?]. "IOVESIVS" is set in small capitals in the original. The "Hic" at lower right is a catchword, not a note. The initial "A" of "Audax" and "Q" of "Quòd" are decorated letters. No greek or hebrew on the page.</notes>
</page>
